```js
// 1️⃣ Define the helper that checks the department
function getSales(record) {
  return record.department === 'Sales';
}

// 2️⃣ Call the tool to fetch the matching records
fetchSalesDepartmentRecords({
  databaseName: 'employeeRecords',
  queryFunction: "function(record) { return getSales(record); }"
});
```

**Tool invocation**

```json
{
  "name": "fetchSalesDepartmentRecords",
  "arguments": {
    "databaseName": "employeeRecords",
    "queryFunction": "function(record) { return getSales(record); }"
  }
}
```

Make sure `getSales` is defined in the same scope where the tool is executed, so the query function can reference it. This will return all records from `employeeRecords` whose `department` field equals `"Sales"`.

